ay":0.3143,"pass_rate":0.4444,"pass_rate_neutral":0.451,"def_epa_per_play":0.04975},{"week":17,"opponent":"SF","home":false,"pf":7.0,"pa":23.0,"off_snaps":62,"epa_per_play":-0.3046,"pass_rate":0.5645,"pass_rate_neutral":0.4783,"def_epa_per_play":0.03159},{"week":18,"opponent":"TEN","home":true,"pf":25.0,"pa":28.0,"off_snaps":56,"epa_per_play":0.1817,"pass_rate":0.6429,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6087,"def_epa_per_play":0.261}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2024,"team":"TEN","distance":0.4916,"shared":15,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"CAR","distance":0.5097,"shared":15,"play_caller":"Dave Canales"},{"season":2018,"team":"WAS","distance":0.522,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"WAS","distance":0.5255,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2021,"team":"CHI","distance":0.5426,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2022,"team":"CHI","distance":0.5944,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"IND","distance":0.6472,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2018,"team":"MIA","distance":0.7428,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2020,"team":"PHI","distance":0.7485,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2021,"team":"MIN","distance":0.7534,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Texans went 4-13 in 2021 and were outscored 452 to 280. Neither side held up, as the offense ranked 31st in EPA per play and the defense 28th in EPA allowed. Their most distinctive traits were the 3rd highest pistol usage and the 2nd highest Cover 2 rate in the league.","offense":"The Texans offense struggled, ranking 25th or worse in all five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix stayed close to what game situations called for. Their biggest outliers in how they lined up were the 3rd highest pistol usage in the league. Davis Mills ran the passing game and leaned heavily on Brandin Cooks, who drew 26% of the targets.","defense":"The Texans had one of the worst defenses in the league, ranking 26th or worse in four of the five main efficiency measures. Its strongest area was takeaways per game, where it ranked 12th, and its weakest was success rate allowed, where it ranked 31st. Jonathan Greenard led the team with 8 sacks, and Kamu Grugier-Hill added 3, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Schematically, they had the 2nd highest Cover 2 rate in the league.","special":"The Texans were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 78% of field goals, which was well below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the quarterback, about 19% of the money on the books. The offense also turned over more of its roster than most, with 33% of its snaps going to players who were on the team the year before.","players":"Davis Mills played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 2,664 yards. Brandin Cooks was the clear top target with 26% of the looks and 1,037 receiving yards. The backfield was a committee led by Rex Burkhead and Mark Ingram. On defense, Jonathan Greenard led the team with 8 sacks and Desmond King picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"This staff is not in the coaching data, so the comparisons below are based on scheme alone. Their offense looked most like the 2024 Titans and the 2025 Panthers under Dave Canales. Their defense looked most like the 2022 Bears and the 2024 Colts.","trends":"The offense went from 7th in EPA per play in 2020 to 31st in 2021, a big step back. The defense moved from 31st in EPA allowed per play in 2020 to 28th in 2021, a modest improvement. The biggest change in approach was early-down pass rate, which went from 59% to 45%.","notes":"FTN did not start charting plays until 2022, so play action, motion, RPO and screen rates are not available for 2021. Everything else, including personnel, formations and coverage, is complete for this season."}}